PoolCounterRedis: give each client a session ID

$session has been declared but never assigned since the class was added in
1.23. It is the client's member in the pool's Redis wait set, so every
waiter shares a single member. Reproduced with our ArticleView settings
(1 worker, maxqueue 8, timeout 20):

- When the holder releases, one waiter is woken and one takes the freed
  slot. The rest wait out the full 20s timeout, then get stale output or
  an error.
- The wait set never counts more than one, so maxqueue never applies.

With a unique ID, every waiter is answered as soon as the holder releases,
and requests beyond maxqueue get QUEUE_FULL at once. It also stops PHP 8.5's
"Using null as an array offset is deprecated" at PoolCounterRedis.php:281.

Upstream: not reported yet.
Drop:     once upstream assigns $session.

--- a/includes/PoolCounter/PoolCounterRedis.php
+++ b/includes/PoolCounter/PoolCounterRedis.php
@@ -85,6 +85,9 @@
 		$this->pool = RedisConnectionPool::singleton( $conf['redisConfig'] );
 
 		$this->keySha1 = sha1( $this->key );
+		// Local patch: identifies this client in the pool's wait set. Upstream never
+		// assigns it, so every waiter would share one member.
+		$this->session = bin2hex( random_bytes( 16 ) );
 		$met = ini_get( 'max_execution_time' ); // usually 0 in CLI mode
 		$this->lockTTL = $met ? 2 * (int)$met : 3600;
 
